From: claude <claude@p7x.dev>
Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH] mail/notmuch-git: Synchronize Notmuch tags
 through a git repository
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:08:56 +0000

notmuch-git keeps a chosen set of Notmuch tags in a git repository,
so they can be committed, pushed, and merged like any other history.
Tags carrying a configured prefix are written to the repository as
one file per message and tag, and read back into the Notmuch
database on checkout or merge. One person can use it to carry tags
between machines; a group can use it to share a common set of tags,
as the Notmuch project does with nmbug for its bug tracker.

Notmuch ships the script and mail/notmuch already installs its
notmuch-git(1) manual page, but no port installs the script itself,
so "notmuch git" fails with "Unknown command 'git'". It is a slave
port, like mail/notmuch-mutt, so that Python and git stay out of the
dependencies of every mail/notmuch user.

WWW: https://notmuchmail.org/
---
Notes for review:

Followed mail/notmuch-mutt, the other script-only slave of
mail/notmuch, for the slave layout.

Why a new port rather than installing the script from mail/notmuch:
the script needs Python and git at run time, and mail/notmuch has
neither as a run dependency today. Debian makes the same split with
its notmuch-git binary package.

Lines whose purpose is not obvious:
- PORTREVISION=0: mail/notmuch sets PORTREVISION?=1 so that slaves
  can pin their own. Without it the new package starts at 0.40_1 and
  is bumped by every revision of the master. portlint warns that new
  ports should not set PORTREVISION; this is the reason it stays.
- USES=python:run and shebangfix: the script starts with
  "#!/usr/bin/env python3". It uses only the standard library;
  py-notmuch2 is optional (it falls back without it), so it is not a
  dependency.
- NO_BUILD and do-install: the script is installed as is, renamed
  the way upstream's own build names it.
- PORTSCOUT: copied from the master, since the slave tracks the same
  distfile and inherits nothing from the master's .ifndef MASTERDIR
  blocks.

The notmuch-git(1) manual page stays in mail/notmuch, which already
installs it under the MANPAGES option.

Checked: portclippy and portfmt clean; portlint -A has only the
PORTREVISION warning above. Built on 15.1-RELEASE amd64 outside
poudriere: stage, check-plist, and package all pass, and the staged
notmuch-git runs with its shebang rewritten to python3.12. The
package depends on git, notmuch, and python312. Not run under
poudriere testport.

